","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dal_Makhani.jpg"}},"dish/dengke-mas-naniura":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/dengke-mas-naniura","n":"Dengke mas naniura","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Dengke mas naniura is a traditional Batak dish originating from the North Sumatra province of Indonesia. The name of the dish means \"pickled fish\" in the Toba Batak language. The dish is made with raw carp which is soaked in Kaffir limes and seasoned with andaliman. According to local oral tradition, only Batak kings were allowed to eat the dish, but in modern times there is no such restriction."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-dengke-mas-naniura"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dengke_mas_naniura"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":10,"links":[["Andaliman","ingredient/andaliman"],["Candlenut","ingredient/candlenut"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Chili powder","ingredient/chili-powder"],["Common carp","ingredient/common-carp"],["Etlingera elatior","ingredient/etlingera-elatior"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Lime","ingredient/lime"],["Red onion","ingredient/red-onion"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","ref":"site/dailycookingquest-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","